# Review: Echo

The namespace-module surface is solid: Relation, Ref, Entity, Query, Filter, Order, Aggregate, Registry, Scope,
Migration, Text, Blob, Annotation, Json, JsonSchema, Collection, Tag and View export what the spec lists, and the
query, Effect and serialization behaviour is tested here and in `@dxos/echo-client` / `echo-client-e2e`. Feature
F-7 (feed options) is now built: the `Feed` object carries optional `indexing` and `retention` fields,
`IndexingOptions` and `RetentionOptions` are schemas with the specified bounds, and `setIndexing` / `setRetention`
validate and write in one `Obj.update`; `Feed.test.ts` and `echo-client` `feed.test.ts` run scenario T-6.
Remaining divergences are in the older API lists: `Obj.getSchema`, `Obj.getDXN`, `Type.isMutable`,
`Database.runQuery` / `schemaQuery` / `runSchemaQuery` and `Feed.cursor` / `next` / `nextOption` do not exist,
`Format` has no `string`/`number`/... members, and `Obj.fromJSON` takes `{ refResolver, database }` rather than
`{ graph, db }`. Scenario T-3 conflicts with the code: a query subscription does not fire when a matched object
is mutated without changing the result set.

Of 54 items: 40 done, 5 untested, 7 partial, 1 diverged, 1 missing (T-4).

